    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **256 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `membershipNumber` is a derived, read-only field, so I followed the existing pattern used for `displayName`/`initials` (computed in the mapper, no new DB column):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the JSON response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `formatMembershipNumber(owner)`, mapped onto `toOwnerDto`. It builds `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'` where `YY` is the registration-date year mod 100, zero-padded (`String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, year % 100)`), yielding e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`. It returns `null` when `customerCode` or `registrationDate` is absent, keeping seed/other-endpoint owners safe from NPEs.\n\nSince `customerCode` and `registrationDate` are already populated on create (and persisted) by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, the value is correct on both the create response and subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}`.",
